## Milestone Rules

Based on the scene design and task sequence, here are the milestone completion criteria:

```json
{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "chop_trees",
      "task": "chop trees",
      "description": "Player has chopped at least one oak tree, obtaining oak logs in their inventory",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "inventory_has",
          "item": "oak_log",
          "quantity": 1,
          "comparison": "gte"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "craft_coal_block",
      "task": "craft to coal_block",
      "description": "Player has crafted a coal block using 9 coal at the crafting table",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "inventory_has",
          "item": "coal_block",
          "quantity": 1,
          "comparison": "gte"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "interact_with_brewingstand",
      "task": "interact with brewingstand",
      "description": "Player has interacted with the brewing stand by opening its GUI (right-clicking it). Detected by the player being within interaction range of the brewing stand and the brewing stand being used.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_inside_box",
          "min": [-4, -1, 2],
          "max": [0, 2, 6],
          "description": "Player is within interaction range of the brewing stand at (~-2, 0, 4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "inventory_changed",
          "description": "Detects that the player has interacted with the brewing stand. Since we cannot directly detect GUI opening, we use proximity as the primary indicator combined with the sequential dependency that coal_block must be crafted first."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

